# Project instructions

- Read `.gig/JOB.md` before working. Price and payment facts come only from `.gig/QUOTE.md`; quotes in old reports are void.
- Original materials are read-only{% if material_path %}: `{{ material_path }}`{% endif %}. Copy needed samples to `data/samples/`; client samples are never committed.
- New results go to new directories, never overwriting old ones; failures and unusable states stay visible.
- At the end of every phase append to "Status" in `.gig/JOB.md`: commands, verification figures, commit / CI run, remaining work, whether anything was sent out.
- Temporary files and recovery copies go in `.scratch/`, cleared at the end of a phase. Create nothing in the parent directory.
- Actions that need JC's explicit approval: sending anything out, pushing to a remote, deleting or archiving, paid remote resources, scope changes beyond the confirmed decisions, edits to `.gig/QUOTE.md`.
- ASCII punctuation in prose. English directory and file names. Explain concepts with concrete names, no undefined abbreviations.
- Reports use Kami or LaTeX; keep only the final PDF; sources in `.scratch/reports/`, prose through sepia.
- Commit each verified unit of work locally; pushing needs separate authorisation.

## Tool projects

- Cross-platform: develop and verify on Linux; clients mostly run Windows. No Windows-only technology. Python with uv and pyproject, ruff, pytest.
- Every configuration item can be overridden on the command line. Tools for non-technical clients read an ini file next to the program (UTF-8, commented in the client's language) and generate it with defaults when absent.
- Inputs: files, directories (recursive), zip. Outputs go to a new directory, originals untouched, with a processing report. Anomalies go into the report with a notice; what can be processed still is.
- Deliverable programs are PyInstaller onefile builds from GitHub Actions (windows-latest and ubuntu-latest) in a private repository; JOB.md records the run id and commit. Pushing to that repository needs JC's authorisation.
- Before delivery rerun this batch's inputs with the CI-built program and compare byte for byte with the source run. Windows interaction (drag and drop, double click, dialogs) that was only smoke-tested on CI is stated in JOB.md and in the manual's known limitations.
- Client documents: a manual PDF in the client's language (Kami, with screenshots), plus a separate developer README.

